{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1443438-house-rule-entanglements","id":1443438,"title":"House Rule: Entanglements","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-04-10T19:46:18-07:00","id":1443438,"title":"House Rule: Entanglements","content":"I am looking for some feedback on a house rule I am thinking about trying to do in my v5 campaign. Basically the idea would be that the actions of the players would risk an increase in the overall hostile nature of the city that would result. The system is based on the entanglements rule from Blades in the Dark which I think is a really good fit. I stole the threat levels from Fall of London as well but would expand them to just include all citywide conflict. I also stole from the anarchs book chart pretty liberally. It can also be used as inspiration just to mess with your players. Tell me what you guys think and give me some ideas to flesh it out!<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Heat: Heat is rated one to ten. When it hits ten it increases to the next level. It starts as zero. PCs can take actions to decrease heat.</li> <li>At the end of every session roll a d10 according to the current heat. Use the result to add additional complications to the coterie for the next session.</li> <li>How to increase heat<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>0-6 based on how explosive the session was overall. 0 for quiet and good. 6 for explosive and violent.</li> <li>2 for the death of mortals during the session. Increase for more newsworthy cases decrease for less. Ie 3 for the death of a police officer 1 for a runaway with no connections</li> <li>1 heat if it happened in hostile territory.</li> <li>1 heat if the sects are in open war</li> </ol></li> <li>Threat Level 0<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>No rolls</li> </ol></li> <li>Threat Level 1<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Minion trouble: One of your backgrounds gets themselves in trouble that will need to be resolved</li> <li>Recruit them: A powerful NPC reaches down to the players and makes them an offer to come work for them.</li> <li>Pay them off: A powerful NPC whos interests have been hurt by the players makes them an offer to back off permanently</li> <li>Study Them: A major organization dispatches an agent to spy on the PCs</li> <li>Rat Them out: Another organization leaks info to a mortal organization to tangle up the PCs</li> <li>Rough them up: A powerful organization sends a group to rough up one of the PCs as a warning</li> <li>Rival: A previously neutral kindred makes a move on one of your assets</li> <li>Interrogation: Police pull in people for questioning about one of the PCs escapades</li> <li>Cooperation: Another vampire you have a good relationship with asks for a favor or you will lose favor with them.</li> <li>Street law: A beat cop begins an investigation into one of the PCs actions</li> </ol></li> <li>Threat Level 2<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Frame Job: A rival of the coterie targets an enemy of the coterie and frames the PCs</li> <li>Lure them away: A powerful organization creates a problem elsewhere that the PCs will need to deal with</li> <li>Isolate them: A powerful organization goes after a friend or family member of a PC</li> <li>Heavy hitter: Someone dispatches a heavy hitter to rough up the PCs</li> <li>Unquiet Dead: The victim of some recent PC involvement Begins to haunt one of the PCs</li> <li>Show of force: A rival vampire makes a move on one of your PCs territory</li> <li>Arrest: One of your ghouls, allies or contacts has an arrest warrant issued for them.</li> <li>Detective squad: A detective is assigned a case of one of the PCs actions</li> <li>Solo: A lone hunter catches the trail of one of the PCs</li> <li>Media spotlight: An enterprising Journalist writes up a piece that puts one of the PCs holdings in a bad light</li> </ol></li> <li>Threat Level 3<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Promote them: Offer power and wealth to change their ways and defect</li> <li>Starve them: Increase pressure on the PCs territory</li> <li>Flipped: One of your backgrounds swaps allegiance to one of your rivals</li> <li>Cell: A hunter cell begins tracking one of the PCs</li> <li>Federal involvement: The FBI takes the notice of one of the PCs actions</li> </ol></li> <li>Threat Level 4<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Hit team: Hunter team dispatched by the second inquisition</li> <li>Politics: Blood Hunt is to be discussed at a primogen meeting</li> <li>Wake them up: Target a haven for destruction</li> </ol></li> <li>Threat Level 5<br /> <ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Blood Hunt</li> <li>Second Inquisition: Full on citywide manhunt for the PCs by the second inquisition</li> </ol></li> </ol>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-11T13:21:48-07:00","id":1443500,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s an interesting concept and it\u2019s the kind of thing I might adapt for my own games! I\u2019m not a crunch-head so my only suggestion might be that some of the lower level threat responses feel like they should be in response to higher threat scores but aside from that I think it\u2019s interesting. Hope you continue to work on it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}